cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SeVim in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "SeVim: Deterministic Semantic-to-Visual Mapping for Educational Diagrams"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kermani Kolankeh"
    given-names: "Arash"
    affiliation: "School of Engineering, Applied Science, and Technology (SEAST), Canadian University Dubai"
    email: arash.kolankeh@cud.ac.ae
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arashkermaniprojects/sevim"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
type: software
abstract: >
  SeVim is a five-stage neuro-symbolic pipeline that converts natural-language
  educational text into deterministic, byte-reproducible SVG diagrams without
  hallucination and without external API calls. It combines a rule-based
  semantic triple extractor, a frozen Qwen2.5-7B encoder, and a deterministic
  Sugiyama layout engine.
keywords:
  - knowledge graph
  - SVG generation
  - educational technology
  - neuro-symbolic
  - deterministic layout
  - information visualization
